   "source": [
    "# Car Insurance Claim Prediction - Exploratory Data Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e21030e6-5216-425c-a13d-336e2fe05ca8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Batch Details"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1dc0762e-d78d-4ec2-acba-a3b59814c4a3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Project Description:** \\\n",
    "This project aims to build a predictive model to identify whether a car policyholder will file an insurance claim in the next 6 months. By prdicting the likelihood of a claim, the insurance company can better manage risk, set appropriate preimiums and optimize its reserve.\\\n",
    "**Business Context**\\\n",
    "The car insurance claims represents a sgnificant cost centre for insurers. Identifying high-risk profiles allows for dynamic pricing and Targeted interventions. The dataset consists of three parts:\\\n",
    "\n",
    "    1. Policy Features : Information about the policyholder and the policy.\n",
    "    2. Car Features: Detailed technical specifications of the insured vehicle.\n",
    "    3. Insurance Claim: The target variable indicating if a claim was filled.\n",
    "\n",
    "In this notebook we perform a comprehensive Exploratory Data Analysis(EDA) to understand the data, assess its quality, and uncover patterns that will inform our modelling strategy.\\\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7cbb97d9-c9fb-4086-ab33-fc3ab1e3946a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Phase 1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 111,
   "id": "e41477b6-7b34-4f45-a190-cdfb4e163e5b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "All Libraries are imported successfully\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import scipy.stats as stats\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "import re\n",
    "\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "print(\"All Libraries are imported successfully\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "df379fda-983d-4875-a4c3-55582344a984",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Data Loading Approach**\\\n",
    "We have three seperate Excel files containing our data . we will load each file into its own pandas Dataframe. This allows us to inspect the raw structure and dimensions of each dataset before combining them. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 112,
   "id": "46328c4e-46c3-4053-8121-738f2a1ab08c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
