   "source": [
    "quality_report = pd.DataFrame(index=df.columns)\n",
    "quality_report['Data Type'] = df.dtypes\n",
    "quality_report['Missing Values'] = df.isnull().sum()\n",
    "quality_report['Missing %'] = (df.isnull().sum() / len(df) * 100).round(2)\n",
    "quality_report['Unique Values'] = df.nunique()\n",
    "def calculate_health(row):\n",
    "    score = 100\n",
    "    score -= row['Missing %']\n",
    "    if row['Missing %'] > 50 : score -= 20\n",
    "    if row['Unique Values'] == 1: score -= 50\n",
    "    return max(0, score)\n",
    "\n",
    "quality_report['Health Score / 100'] = quality_report.apply(calculate_health, axis=1)\n",
    "display(quality_report.sort_values(by='Health Score / 100').style.background_gradient(cmap='RdYlGn', subset=['Health Score / 100']))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "06f6572f-1fac-4cf1-b95c-ecc02feb1f74",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Conclusion:** The dataset shows excellent overall data quality. All variables have health scores between 99.96 and 100, with no columns exceeding the 50% missing-value threshold and no constant columns detected. Missing data is minimal, with the highest missingness found in fuel_type (26 values, approximately 0.04%) and policy_tenure (20 values, approximately 0.03%). Most columns are complete, and the dataset contains both numeric and categorical variables suitable for further analysis."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "aa3b6a57-a253-417e-9007-d0370790aea7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Phase 4\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "90c4d89a-6f07-4a76-834a-76eb6073224b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "we will now execute the cleaning steps. We will create a fresh copy (df_clean) to preserve the raw merged data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 124,
   "id": "bcbd9440-6cb0-4d2f-a10b-5fb14eca5386",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Columns renamed successfully \n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df_clean = df.copy()\n",
    "rename_dict = {\n",
    "    'ebgine_type': 'engine_type',\n",
    "    'is_adjustable_steer': 'is_adjustable_steering',\n",
    "    'is_driver_seat_height_ajustable': 'is_driver_seat_height_adjustable'\n",
    "}\n",
    "df_clean = df_clean.rename(columns=rename_dict)\n",
    "print(\"Columns renamed successfully \")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "39dbf37b-85f8-4fec-8f86-14a5e0dce3bc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Column Renaming**\n",
    "We standardise the column names based on the expected data dictionary. This ensures consistency and prevents KeyErrors when selecting features downstream."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 125,
   "id": "0be5ca28-4b6f-45ca-90ba-95256e273ff2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "BEFORE cleaning 'is_esc':\n",
      "is_esc\n",
      "No     40145\n",
      "Yes    18367\n",
      "NaN        3\n",
      "Name: count, dtype: int64\n",
      "\n",
      "AFTER cleaning 'is_esc':\n",
      "is_esc\n",
      "0.0    40145\n",
      "1.0    18367\n",
      "NaN        3\n",
      "Name: count, dtype: int64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "bool_cols_updated = [rename_dict.get(col, col) for col in bool_cols_raw]\n",
    "def clean_boolean(val):\n",
    "    if pd.isna(val):\n",
    "        return np.nan\n",
    "    if isinstance(val, str):\n",
    "        val = val.strip().upper()\n",
    "        if val == 'YES':\n",
    "            return 1.0\n",
    "        elif val == 'NO':\n",
    "            return 0.0\n",
    "        elif val == '':\n",
    "            return np.nan\n",
    "    return val\n",
    "sample_col = 'is_esc'\n",
    "if sample_col in df_clean.columns:\n",
    "    print(f\"BEFORE cleaning '{sample_col}':\")\n",
    "    print(df_clean[sample_col].value_counts(dropna=False))\n",
    "for col in bool_cols_updated:\n",
    "    if col in df_clean.columns:\n",
    "        df_clean[col] = df_clean[col].apply(clean_boolean)\n",
    "if sample_col in df_clean.columns:\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nAFTER cleaning '{sample_col}':\")\n",
    "    print(df_clean[sample_col].value_counts(dropna=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "042c7698-8cbe-4e12-a9d8-133a564ee987",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Boolean Cleaning**\n",
    "In this step the cleaning function strips leading/trailing whitespaces, converts strings to uppercase to handle case variations ('yes', 'YES'), maps them to numeric floats (1.0/0.0), and converts empty strings or pure whitespaces to explicitly represent missing values (NaN)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
