    "**Bivariate Analysis (Policy Features vs Insurance Claim)** \n",
    "\n",
    "Now we transition to bivariate analysis, where we investigate the relationship between independent variables and our target variable, is_claim. In this section, we focus on policy and policyholder-related features to see how they impact the likelihood of a claim."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "35930024-909a-4291-95af-dc8becffeb32",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**6.1 policy_tenure vs is_claim**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 136,
   "id": "0fb3008b-9a00-42ae-8c75-b218846f13c4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1800x500 with 3 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "COLORS = {\n",
    "    'bg':       '#00A3E0',\n",
    "    'no_claim': '#E8A317',\n",
    "    'claim':    '#4C72B0',\n",
    "}\n",
    "COLORS['palette'] = [COLORS['no_claim'], COLORS['claim']]\n",
    "CLAIM_LABELS = ['No Claim', 'Claim']\n",
    "\n",
    "def relabel_legend(ax):\n",
    "    handles = ax.get_legend_handles_labels()[0]\n",
    "    if handles:\n",
    "        ax.legend(handles, CLAIM_LABELS, title='Claim Status')\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(18, 5))\n",
    "fig.patch.set_facecolor(COLORS['bg'])\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.boxplot(x='is_claim', y='policy_tenure', data=df_clean,\n",
    "            hue='is_claim', palette=COLORS['palette'],\n",
    "            legend=True, ax=axes[0])\n",
    "axes[0].set_title('Box Plot of Policy Tenure by Claim', fontsize=12)\n",
    "relabel_legend(axes[0])\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.violinplot(x='is_claim', y='policy_tenure', data=df_clean,\n",
    "               hue='is_claim', palette=COLORS['palette'],\n",
    "               legend=True, ax=axes[1])\n",
    "axes[1].set_title('Violin Plot of Policy Tenure by Claim', fontsize=12)\n",
    "relabel_legend(axes[1])\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.kdeplot(data=df_clean[df_clean['is_claim'] == 0]['policy_tenure'],\n",
    "            color=COLORS['no_claim'], label='No Claim', fill=True, ax=axes[2])\n",
    "sns.kdeplot(data=df_clean[df_clean['is_claim'] == 1]['policy_tenure'],\n",
    "            color=COLORS['claim'], label='Claim', fill=True, ax=axes[2])\n",
    "axes[2].set_title('KDE Plot of Policy Tenure by Claim', fontsize=12)\n",
    "axes[2].legend(title='Claim Status')\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Policy Tenure vs Is_Claim', fontsize=16, fontweight='bold', y=1.05)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9b33c9b9-c36b-4219-aaa3-f062f1f9204f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Inference(policy_tenure vs is_claim)**\n",
    "\n",
    "    . Higher tenure among claimants: Policyholders who filed a claim (is_claim = 1) tend to have a higher median policy tenure (~0.83) than those who didn't (~0.55). The claim group's box sits higher overall, suggesting claims are somewhat more common among longer-tenured policies.\n",
    "    . Wider spread for non-claimants: The \"No Claim\" group spans a broader range (roughly 0.2–1.03 in the IQR) and reaches down to the lowest tenures, while claimants are more concentrated in the mid-to-high tenure range (~0.4–1.08).\n",
    "    . Distribution shape (violin/KDE): Both groups are bimodal, with peaks near the low end (~0.1) and the high end (~1.1). The \"No Claim\" group has a much taller low-tenure peak, meaning many non-claim policies are new/short-tenured. Claimants are relatively more concentrated at higher tenure.\n",
    "    . Takeaway: Policy tenure has a modest positive association with claims — short-tenure policies skew toward no claim, while longer-tenure policies show a higher share of claims. The overlap is large, so tenure alone is a weak separator and should be combined with other features for prediction."
   ]
  },
