   "source": [
    "**Inference (Age of Car vs Is Claim)**\n",
    "\n",
    "    . Nearly identical distributions: Both claim and no-claim groups have the same low median car age (~0.05) and overlap almost completely in the KDE plot and the two curves are barely distinguishable.\n",
    "    . Right-skewed, mostly new cars: Both groups are heavily concentrated at low car age (0–0.15) with a long thin tail, meaning most vehicles are relatively new regardless of claim status. \n",
    "    . More outliers in non-claim group: The \"No Claim\" box shows more high-age outliers (up to ~1.0), while claimants top out lower (~0.4).\n",
    "    . Takeaway: Car age shows almost no separation between claim and no-claim groups so it's a weak predictor on its own and adds little discriminative value for the claim model."
   ]
