   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ca81bf1c-8ff5-47fb-9327-85483892e9fd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**7.6 Boolean Safety Features vs is_claim**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 146,
   "id": "da51a345-5ab9-46c9-86ad-25a4d1374c63",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1000x1200 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate claim rates for feature=1 vs feature=0\n",
    "safety_impact = []\n",
    "global_mean = df_clean['is_claim'].mean() * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "for col in bool_cols:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        rates = df_clean.groupby(col)['is_claim'].mean() * 100\n",
    "        rate_0 = rates.get(0, np.nan)\n",
    "        rate_1 = rates.get(1, np.nan)\n",
    "        diff = rate_1 - rate_0\n",
    "        safety_impact.append({\n",
    "            'Feature': col,\n",
    "            'Rate_Absent(0)': rate_0,\n",
    "            'Rate_Present(1)': rate_1,\n",
    "            'Difference (1 - 0)': diff\n",
    "        })\n",
    "    except:\n",
    "        pass\n",
    "\n",
    "df_safety = pd.DataFrame(safety_impact).dropna().sort_values(by='Difference (1 - 0)')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plotting\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 12))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Positions for the bars\n",
    "y = np.arange(len(df_safety))\n",
    "height = 0.35\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.barh(y - height/2, df_safety['Rate_Absent(0)'], height, label='Absent (0)', color='#e74c3c')\n",
    "ax.barh(y + height/2, df_safety['Rate_Present(1)'], height, label='Present (1)', color='#2ecc71')\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_yticks(y)\n",
    "ax.set_yticklabels(df_safety['Feature'])\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Claim Rate (%)', fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax.set_title('Claim Rate by Safety Feature Presence vs Absence', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax.axvline(global_mean, color='k', linestyle='--', label='Global Avg')\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "32d68538-e05e-4805-a665-b901e0742c45",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Inference**\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Consistent, counterintuitive pattern: for every feature, Present (green, =1) has a higher claim rate than Absent (red, =0). Safety features are associated with more claims, not fewer.\n",
    "    Strongest gaps (biggest 1−0 difference): is_speed_alert, is_parking_sensors, is_adjustable_steering, Absent sits well below the global mean (~4.1%, ~5.4%, ~6.0%), Present sits at/above it.\n",
    "    Modeling takeaway: individually each gap is modest, but the uniform direction suggests a shared latent factor (vehicle segment/price/age). Consider a single \"feature-count\" or trim-level variable rather than 17 correlated binaries and they'll be highly collinear."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2f45fb73-59ce-4ac0-97ea-306c8332feb6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
