   "source": [
    "**Inference**\n",
    "\n",
    "    . All four engine specs show near-identical distributions across claim (1) vs no-claim (0). Medians and IQRs overlap almost completely.\n",
    "    . torque_nm / power_bhp: medians match (~113 Nm, ~88 bhp). Claim group's lower whisker/Q1 reaches slightly lower on power_bhp, but the difference is negligible.\n",
    "    . displacement: claim group's Q1 dips a bit lower (~1000 vs ~800 floor), medians equal (~1200) — trivial.\n",
    "    . cylinder: effectively identical (3–4 range, same box).\n",
    "    . Takeaway: engine characteristics carry no discriminative signal for is_claim. Like the safety/transmission/NCAP features, these are weak standalone predictors and torque/power/displacement/cylinder are almost certainly highly correlated with each other."
   ]
